WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.818
Meet CrossExam.

2
00:00:00.818 --> 00:00:06.953
It finds broken software that your tests accept. then proves whether stronger evaluations actually help.

3
00:00:06.953 --> 00:00:08.754
Here. all four tests pass.

4
00:00:08.754 --> 00:00:12.356
But an optimization drops the tenant from the cache key.

5
00:00:12.356 --> 00:00:17.759
Two customers reuse the same request ID. and the second gets the first customer's reservation.

6
00:00:17.759 --> 00:00:20.281
CrossExam reduces the failure to two requests.

7
00:00:20.281 --> 00:00:22.698
The eval improves through versioned proposals.

8
00:00:22.698 --> 00:00:27.935
Each suite is frozen. then challenged on separate validation defects and correct implementations.

9
00:00:27.935 --> 00:00:29.949
Only measured gains earn promotion.

10
00:00:29.949 --> 00:00:32.367
A deliberately weakened suite is rejected.

11
00:00:32.367 --> 00:00:34.259
Now the final audit opens.

12
00:00:34.259 --> 00:00:40.315
Detection rises from 1 of 8 defects to 7 of 8. with 0 correct controls rejected.

13
00:00:40.315 --> 00:00:42.965
Every result. including remaining misses. is published.

14
00:00:42.965 --> 00:00:45.569
This is the reproducible local benchmark.

15
00:00:45.569 --> 00:00:48.607
Live Meta and Subquadratic adapters are separate.

16
00:00:48.607 --> 00:00:52.948
Every result includes source hashes. frozen tests. and execution traces.

17
00:00:52.948 --> 00:00:53.362
CrossExam.

18
00:00:53.362 --> 00:00:54.603
Your tests passed.

19
00:00:54.603 --> 00:00:55.845
Your software failed.

20
00:00:55.845 --> 00:00:57.500
Here is the evidence.
